# Split ownership for anti-PR-escalation (see .data/specs/roles-and-capabilities.md).
# Replace the placeholder handles with real GitHub usernames or teams at M0.
#
# Superadmin-owned (admins cannot self-promote): roles, CODEOWNERS, CI, and root config.
/CODEOWNERS              @atwellpub @gbtilabs
/.github/                @atwellpub @gbtilabs
/house/roles.yml         @atwellpub @gbtilabs
/astro.config.mjs        @atwellpub @gbtilabs
/package.json            @atwellpub @gbtilabs
/src/                    @atwellpub @gbtilabs
/scripts/                @atwellpub @gbtilabs

# Admin-owned: bans, grandfather, and the rest of house/. The two superadmins own both tiers
# until a separate admin team exists (swap an @org/admins team in here later without touching
# the superadmin-owned paths above).
/house/                  @atwellpub @gbtilabs

# SOW-087: brand-reach controls (the category -> Discord-channel map + the moderation word lists) are
# superadmin-tier by intent; the two superadmins own them explicitly even if /house/ is later delegated.
/house/content-channels.yml  @atwellpub @gbtilabs
/house/moderation-flags.yml  @atwellpub @gbtilabs

# sow-271: the site-wide presentation toggles are superadmin-tier by intent. This pin is what MAKES the
# extension-CTA switch a superadmin setting: without it, "superadmin only" would be a claim the admin UI makes
# and an admin could walk around it with a pull request. The endpoint rank check and this pin are the two
# independent authorities, and the gate is the one that actually merges.
/house/site-settings.yml     @atwellpub @gbtilabs
# sow-312: the newsletter send-rate caps. Pinned explicitly for the same reason as the files above: it is
# already covered by /house/, but this one decides how much mail goes to other people's inboxes and whether
# sending happens at all (daily_cap: 0 is the pause), so the tier should not depend on /house/ staying
# superadmin-owned if it is ever delegated.
/house/mail-settings.yml     @atwellpub @gbtilabs
# sow-266: what the digest says about membership, and who sponsors it. Superadmin for the same reason the
# send caps are: it decides what goes into other people's inboxes, and the sponsor block is a paid placement.
/house/digest-config.yml  @atwellpub @gbtilabs

# sow-298: the syndication templates are superadmin-tier. Their write ops went in superadmin at the op level
# (editHouseYaml -> requireRole superadmin) but this pin was never added, so for this one file the endpoint
# rank was the ONLY real control: the PR gate read it as ordinary /house/ and would not have caught an
# admin-ranked mistake. Pinned by owner ruling 2026-09-01, which ratifies the enforcement rather than
# tightening it. membership/path-rank.mjs carries the matching row and a test holds the two in lockstep.
/house/syndication-config.yml  @atwellpub @gbtilabs

# sow-281: the registered content CTAs (which partner links ride on which content, on whose affiliate tag) are
# superadmin-tier. The CTA write ops are superadmin at the endpoint and this pin is the second authority, so an
# admin cannot attach a paid link to any member's item by pull request. membership/path-rank.mjs carries the
# matching row and test/path-rank.test.mjs holds the two in lockstep.
/house/ctas.yml              @atwellpub @gbtilabs

# sow-359: the tracked partner redirects (house/outbound-links.yml). Where a paying click lands, and on whose
# referral code, is the same kind of decision as which card carries which partner link above. Pinned here,
# in SUPERADMIN_HOUSE_FILES and on the three write ops, so no single layer is the only thing holding it.
/house/outbound-links.yml    @atwellpub @gbtilabs
# sow-338: how much the news pipeline takes from each source. Admins own the source POOL (add, disable, remove) in
# house/news-sources.yml; the weighting is a superadmin's call, which is why it is a separate file: one file cannot
# be owned at two ranks. Pinned here and in SUPERADMIN_HOUSE_FILES, and the Worker's action carries the same rank.
/house/news-source-weights.yml  @atwellpub @gbtilabs
# sow-372: the words that keep a story out of the news stream. Same split as the weights above: admins own which
# publications we read, superadmins own what we refuse to republish. A word added here silences every story
# carrying it, in the feed and in the digest, so it is pinned at the top tier and mirrored in SUPERADMIN_HOUSE_FILES.
/house/news-banwords.yml     @atwellpub @gbtilabs
# sow-337: the call-to-action card images, committed beside house/ctas.yml in the same PR. An image shows on every
# page its card is assigned to, so it is pinned at the registry's tier. membership/path-rank.mjs carries the row.
/house/images/ctas/          @atwellpub @gbtilabs

# SOW-022: applets are a SUPERADMIN-only content type (GBTI does not host member code). Explicit so the rule
# holds even if /house/ is later delegated to an admin team. The collection glob also excludes member folders,
# and validate-content rejects any members/*/applets/.
/house/applets/          @atwellpub @gbtilabs

# members/<username>/ is author-scoped by the gate + scripts/validate-content.mjs, not by CODEOWNERS.
